# {{ component.name }} — Python API backend · Litestar

An application factory, `GET /health`, HTTP boundary tests and an installable src-layout package.
Authentication, persistence, business operations and deployment are intentionally not implemented.

```bash
# From this package directory
uv sync --group dev
uv run pytest -W error
uv build
# Start a loopback development server only when needed
uv run python -m {{ component.module }}
```

Record the resulting `uv.lock` alongside this package. The starter requires Python 3.11 or newer; select a supported
minor version in the actual toolchain/CI. This starter floor is not Litestar's minimum Python requirement.
Exact versions were checked against PyPI on 2026-10-26:
[Litestar 2.25.0](https://pypi.org/project/litestar/2.25.0/),
[Uvicorn 0.54.0](https://pypi.org/project/uvicorn/0.54.0/),
[HTTPX 0.28.1](https://pypi.org/project/httpx/0.28.1/).
The native Litestar test client uses HTTPX; FastAPI's separate test-client dependency choice does not apply here.

## Ownership

- `src/{{ component.module }}/app.py`: application composition and HTTP boundary. Add a router/controller when routes
  need shared configuration or independent ownership, not to fill an empty architecture.
- `src/{{ component.module }}/__main__.py`: optional guarded development entrypoint. Importing it starts no server.
- `tests/test_health.py`: software-only status/payload and unknown-route smoke, not product acceptance or readiness.
- `pyproject.toml`/`uv.lock`: this package's environment. No ORM, queue or external DI container is selected.
- Real clients/tasks acquire and release resources through explicit dependency/lifespan owners when needed.

